  "brief": "ICEYE is acquiring Avio for over €2 billion, while AMD has completed its $8.2 billion acquisition of World Labs and Aon has acquired USI for $17 billion.\n\nICEYE / Avio (Announced): ICEYE and Avio Deal. ICEYE is acquiring Avio for over €2 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal is expected to be completed once Vega C rocket's satellite launch capacity is increased [5]. The takeover bid was launched by ICEYE [4].\nDoorDash / Instacart (Pending approval): DoorDash and Instacart Deal. DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal [9, 10, 12]. The deal is currently pending approval from the Justice Department [6, 7, 8]. No new information is available on the status of the deal [13, 11].\nAir Water Ventures / Proud Source Water (Announced): Air Water Ventures Acquires Proud Source Water. Air Water Ventures is acquiring Proud Source Water [15, 16, 17]. The deal is expected to close in 2027 [16]. The acquisition is valued at up to $150M [15].\nTPG / Bill Holdings (Rumored): TPG and Bill Holdings. TPG is reportedly considering a buyout of Bill Holdings [18, 19, 20]. The deal is still in the rumored stage [18, 19, 20].\nAMD / World Labs (Completed): AMD Buys World Labs for $8.2B. AMD has acquired World Labs [21, 22, 24]. The deal is now completed [21, 22, 24]. No further information is available [22, 23, 24].\nAon / USI (Completed): Aon and USI Acquisition. Aon has acquired USI [25, 26, 27]. The deal is worth $17 billion [25, 26, 27]. The acquisition is now complete [26, 27, 28].\nBird / Kel-Gor (Announced): Bird to Buy Kel-Gor. Bird is buying industrial contractor Kel-Gor [29, 30, 31]. The deal was announced by Bird [29, 30, 31].\nTenax Aerospace / Air Industries (Pending approval): Tenax Aerospace and Air Industries Deal. Tenax Aerospace and Air Industries are merging [32, 33]. The deal is pending approval [32]. Shareholders of Air Industries will vote on the merger on November 18 [32].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Integer Holdings completes merger, deregisters unsold S-8 shares [34].\n- Variman Global Enterprises approves preferential share and warrant allotment [35].\n- Nvidia Taps Heidrick & Struggles for CEO Search: WSJ [36].",
